                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really wanted to like this game. I had heard a lot about it, and it sounded interesting to me. Unfortunately, I was disappointed. Sure, the game had good points too. The graphics were decent (even quite good for how old they are) The music is nice, there are lots of settings to chose from, and the voice acting is decent most of the time.\n\nSo why don't I reccomend it? It's far too easy. Every single puzzle revolves around two concepts [spoiler] playing a melody forward (activating the melody spell) or backwards (doing the opposite of the spell) [/spoiler]\n\nSure. Getting your first spell might be a bit tricky, since you don't know where to go, and there are a few sections that are interesting, but I finished the game in about two hours, without a guide (World record run is 24 minutes) and most of that time wasn't trying to figure anything out, but instead simply walking to the next point.\n\nIt is a beautiful game, but far too easy. I got a few nice moments from it, but would have gotten them more efficiently by simply watching a playthrough.",
